Z||000000||Dough19||12-10-2001||02:45 PM||||A friend of mine has a pile of rotors that he is throwing away and he is sure that some of them are for a 88 Fiero. Does anyone know some dimentions that I could measure? The outside diameter, thickness, center hole, offset? Thanks for any help||||reg||3
Z||000001||Spiff||12-11-2001||01:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dough19:<BR><B>A friend of mine has a pile of rotors that he is throwing away and he is sure that some of them are for a 88 Fiero. Does anyone know some dimentions that I could measure? The outside diameter, thickness, center hole, offset? Thanks for any help</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 88 rotors will be vented. All other years were solid. Hope that helps. If he has any extra after you get yours. Since they are getting thrown away. Can I get 4 88 style rotors? I'll pay for shipping.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiffsig2_10.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||watts||12-11-2001||01:16 AM||||I posted this before, but...<P>If you're neeeding rear 88' rotor's, just use the front rotor's from a '93 Cavalier.<P>This swap doesn't work on the front BTW.<P>Make sure your calipers are floating nicely on the pins, and you should be fine.<BR>||||reg||1
